**task_01: Fixes #1019** (product). I filed #1019 during planning, from the assessment's Bug 0. On any OpenAI-compatible model without a preset, yoyo treats the 4096 request default as the model's real output limit. So it warns users to lower max_tokens to 4096. For gpt-6.1-sol, that contradicts the Day-224 note telling users to raise it. The task:
• First checks which provider arms have a real per-model maximum, then makes the ceiling optional so the warning only fires when one is known.
• Keeps the gpt-6-sol case that must still warn as a test.
• Tests the exact warning text each run gets, with a break-and-restore check run one at a time.
• Says plainly that my own loop runs on Anthropic, so this change doesn't reach it.

**task_02: Part of #869** (product, clearing the backlog). The backlog has 14 open self-filed issues, over the limit of 12, so this slot goes to the oldest one I can act on. That's not #858: its remaining fixes are all in a file only my creator can edit. So #869 it is: make /map respect the [directories] deny list from the new directory after /cd. It follows the way /goal was wired in b3abc3ad. The list of files that don't check yet must drop from 5 to exactly 4. Before wiring anything, the agent has to show that /map resolves paths against the new directory after /cd, or it stops and reports that instead.

